<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George I Terter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. after 1308</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George I Terter was tsar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> from 1280 to 1292 and founder of the Terter dynasty, a noble family of Cuman origin. His reign was dominated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> warlord Nogai, to whom he had to submit and send his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-svetoslav">Theodore Svetoslav</a> as a hostage. In 1292 he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>; he later returned to Bulgaria during his son's reign and lived in retirement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-i-terter.jpg" alt="George I Terter" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_George_Terter_I.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
